# The wrapping operators `+%` / `-%` / `*%` produce DEFINED two's-complement
# wraparound at `int` (64-bit) width (todo/t1410).
#
# ⚠ UNARY `-` IS NOT HERE, AND ITS ABSENCE IS DELIBERATE. `-INT64_MIN` is
# signed-overflow UB in C too, but WHAT it should do is unratified: at HEAD
# `0 - INT64_MIN` traps `T_Overflow` while `-INT64_MIN` silently wraps, because
# `Inst::Neg` carries no `Overflow` field and so has no policy at all. Pinning
# the current value in a TOP-LEVEL fixture would enter it into
# `runtime_parity_corpus` and the sanitize sweep, i.e. ratify by fixture a
# value that may flip. The repro lives in `known_gaps/t1443_neg_overflow.gg`
# with an `#[ignore]`d test; the ruling is todo/t1443.
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS FIXTURE IS 64-BIT ONLY, AND WHERE THE REST OF THE AXIS LIVES.
# The full typed axis (3 operators x 4 widths x {signed, unsigned} = 24 cells)
# is `known_gaps/t1410_wrapping_ops_axis.gg`, which is parked
# there FOR PLACEMENT: `runtime_parity_corpus` auto-scans every top-level
# `*.gg`, and the SELF-HOST lane still treats every narrow integer as int64
# (MEASURED: `i8_add` -> 128 not -128, `u8_add` -> 256 not 0, `u64_sub` -> -1
# not 18446744073709551615 -- the great majority of the narrow cells diverge).
# That is todo/t0655's narrow-width gap, still open on the self-host. Booking
# those rows top-level would raise `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING` for this
# round's own inflow, which Core #9 forbids. The three cells BELOW were
# measured MATCHING on the self-host lane, so they belong top-level and the
# rest does not.
#
# TWO INSTRUMENTS PIN THIS FILE, and it is top-level so BOTH can reach it:
#   1. THE VALUES — `wrapping_ops_defined` in tests/integration.rs.
#   2. THE DEFINED-NESS — `scripts/sanitize_sweep.sh` at `UBSAN_CEILING=0`.
#      The corpus is "the top-level `*.gg` plus every `*.gg` under an IN
#      directory", and every manifest directory is currently OUT, so top-level
#      placement IS the sweep pin. MEASURED: reverting the fix takes the sweep
#      from `ubsan: 0` to `ubsan: 1` naming this fixture.
#
# ⚠ THE VALUE PIN ALONE IS NOT COVERAGE. Before the fix the C backend emitted a
# plain SIGNED `+`/`-`/`*` for `Overflow::Wrap` -- undefined in C on overflow --
# and every value below was ALREADY CORRECT and byte-identical. What was wrong
# was the licence the emitted C handed the optimizer at -O2. No stdout
# assertion can see that, in either direction; the UBSan lane is the only
# instrument that can (Core #13).
#
# ⚠ AND THE OPERANDS MUST BE NON-CONSTANT. `z()` is a runtime-computed 0. With
# literals the whole expression is constant-folded, the arithmetic never runs,
# and the probe is green for a reason unrelated to what it tests (SIX-Q #6).

int z():
    String s = ""
    return s.byte_len()


void main():
    int k = z()
    print(f"i64_add={9223372036854775807 + k +% (1 + k)}")
    print(f"i64_sub={-9223372036854775807 - 1 + k -% (1 + k)}")
    print(f"i64_mul={(4611686018427387904 + k) *% (3 + k)}")
